ta><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>IRIE TOHRU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OTA MASASHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SANGO CO LTD</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IRIE, TOHRU</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OTA, MASASHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SANGO CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>IRIE TOHRU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OTA MASASHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IRIE, TOHRU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OTA, MASASHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A production method for a double-structure container having a clearance between an inner tube and an outer tube thereof, wherein, in order to facilitate production thereof and reduce production costs, an inner tube (4A) is disposed inside an outer tube (4B) with a clearance (4C) therebetween, solid inclusion (4D) is held in at least one tube-axis-direction segment in the clearance (4C), and the outer tube (4B) is subjected to spinning in that condition to concurrently change the sections of the inner and outer tubes (4A, 4B).</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un procédé permettant de produire un conteneur présentant une structure double et comprenant un espace séparant un tube intérieur d'un tube extérieur. Pour faciliter la production de ce conteneur et la rendre moins coûteuse, on place un tube (4A) intérieur dans un tube (4B) extérieur, de manière qu'un espace (4C) libre soit ménagé entre les deux. On introduit un produit (4D) d'inclusion solide dans au moins une partie de l'espace (4C) compris dans direction axiale des tubes, et on soumet le tube (4B) externe à un tournage de manière à modifier simultanément les sections (4A, 4B) du tube intérieur et du tube extérieur.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>